KZ3 patch 1123 (SPU pass 105): upstream ps3recomp PR #420 by tekulvw (MIT), "resident code and interpreter
rejoining": overlay residency verified once per load, then dispatch by residency.

- spu_lifted_lookup (the interpreter's rejoin probe and the drain's rejoin test) now resolves with the ownership order
  indirect dispatch uses: a bounded resident code span (authoritative: a miss there stays a miss, a span registered
  with its code bytes is compared once per load and rejected on a mismatch), then the resident task, the resident
  overlay, the primary image. spu_indirect_branch delegates to it.
- New spu_overlay_register_verified_region (spu_overlay_residency.h): a streamed overlay registered with the code
  bytes it was lifted from; a GET from its source EA to its load address marks it pending, the first dispatch into
  the span compares the bytes, any later GET into the span resets (continuation) or clears it.
- The PR's test cases in runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lifted_start.c and its docs/spu-resident-interpreter-rejoin.md.
Adapted to the KZ3 patch set (the hunks that did not apply): patch 1090's spu_ovl_find returns the first matching
source only, so a verified source GET to another load address is ignored (upstream skips to the next source; a
source EA is registered once); spu_indirect_branch keeps patch 1078's located lookup after the shared resolver,
outside resident code spans only (as before); the rejoin probe (patch 1028's overlay probe, 1078's located lookup)
defers to spu_lifted_lookup inside a resident code span; the PR test's g_spu_trampoline_fn line in a helper without
ctx writes c->tramp_fn (patch 1017's macro). KZ3 registers no resident code spans today: the change for KZ3 is the
rejoin's task-then-overlay order. Tests: tools/spu/test_r105_dcache.sh (the PR test, 124 checks with this patch alone).
Upstream: the PR itself.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): #420 upstream: shrinks to nothing but the 1078/1090 pieces above; upstream's per-thread lookup memo (`spu_lookup_memoized`, SPU_TLS) bypassed on MinGW (`spu_lookup` has 1096's process-wide memo; `-DKZ3_SPU_TLS_MEMO` builds it).

